# Gestalt

`gestalt/` is the knowledge base at the workspace root: learned conventions and reference knowledge that persist across sessions, agent-agnostic (Cursor and Claude Code). Full rule text, MANIFEST and GRAPH detail, linking rules and the agent-team note: `gestalt/.cursor/references/gestalt-rule.md`.

## Always Reference Gestalt

Before answering, suggesting an approach, or starting a task, search gestalt and read the entries it points at. Cite what you use: "Per gestalt/knowledge/platform.md, the deploy command is…". This applies to ALL tasks, not only when gestalt is mentioned.

## Lookup

Search first. Never read an index whole: `MANIFEST.md` is about 200 KB. (1) `gestalt_search` finds the entry and `gestalt_route` the skill; then read the one entry, `gestalt/knowledge/<slug>.md` or `gestalt/.cursor/rules/<slug>.mdc`. (2) `gestalt_manifest('<slug>')` for a slug's outgoing `links` and `^block-ids` (paper notes are in `MANIFEST-papers.md`). (3) `GRAPH.md` for cross-cutting data-flow questions, one extra read. (4) `SOURCES.md` when gestalt lacks context, then query Notion, Linear or Slack via MCP. `slug` → `knowledge/slug.md`; `slug` → that line; `slug` → that section. A `slug` with no knowledge file may be a rule under `.cursor/rules/` (2026-08-30); resolve there before calling a link broken. Check for cross-repo entries when a task spans repos.

## Scope: Personal Knowledge Base

`phbui/gestalt` is **personal**. Never write an entry — and never let auto-capture create one — for a repo or system owned by an employer or client, even when the workspace contains it and the entry would be useful: no internal repos, deploy topologies, API contracts, customer data models, access recipes, or incident writeups. Skip silently and say once: "Skipping gestalt capture — work-owned repo." **Generic techniques** learned at work are fine (a library gotcha, a debugging pattern, a Claude Code behavior) provided they carry no internal hostnames, identifiers, credentials, or architecture. A work-system entry found in `knowledge/` gets removed, not redacted.

## Writes

Subject to the scope rule. When you read a **personal** repo's README, Taskfile, or pyproject.toml and no gestalt entry exists, create `gestalt/knowledge/<repo>.md`; rewrite a stale one. When the user corrects a mistake, update gestalt proactively. Don't ask — just do it. Confirm briefly: "Updated gestalt." Check MANIFEST.md before creating an entry; update existing entries rather than duplicate. Use inline `wikilinks` next to the sentence that explains why they relate, `^block-id` anchors on key facts, and `## Data Flow` sections for pipelines. Write philosophy, the mandatory post-write index regeneration and the command execution rules (every step mandatory, no spot checks): `gestalt-operations.md`. Edit `claude-tree/` only, then run `tools/sync-cursor-tree.py --write`; never edit `.cursor/` by hand (`dual-agent-sync.md`). When context nears its limit, run `/save` proactively before the chat is summarized. Command and skill list: `references/skill-index.md`.
